---
import ProjectPage from "../../layouts/ProjectPage.astro";
---

<ProjectPage
    title="Raytheon Drone Competition"
    description="First place in the 2024 Raytheon Drone Competition. Autonomous payload delivery onto a moving target with MAVLink and ArUco markers."
    lede="First place. Autonomous payload delivery onto a moving target."
    figureLabel="Fig. 03 — Raytheon Drone Competition"
    figureAlt="Schematic of a quadrotor, a marker on the ground, and a payload path."
    plate="drone"
    primary={{ href: "#status", label: "Status" }}
    aboutTitle="A moving target."
    sectionId="status"
    sectionTitle="Status."
    sectionLede="The public record is the portfolio line. There is no repository, paper, or build log linked from this site."
>
    <Fragment slot="prose">
        <p>
            2024. First place. Led the team. The system flew autonomous paths
            over MAVLink and used ArUco markers, through OpenCV, to put a
            payload on a moving target. The language named for the work is
            Python.
        </p>
        <p>
            That is the whole public description. This page does not add a
            vehicle, a sensor list, a score, or a procedure that the site
            does not already state.
        </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="facts">
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Year</dt>
            <dd>2024</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Place</dt>
            <dd>1st</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Task</dt>
            <dd>Payload onto a moving target</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Autonomy</dt>
            <dd>MAVLink flight paths</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Markers</dt>
            <dd>ArUco, OpenCV</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Language</dt>
            <dd>Python</dd>
        </div>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="steps">
        <li>
            <p class="t-label">01</p>
            <div class="prose">
                <h3>What the site records</h3>
                <p>
                    Autonomous flight paths over MAVLink. ArUco detection in
                    OpenCV. A payload placed on a moving target. First place,
                    with Yojan leading the team.
                </p>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p class="t-label">02</p>
            <div class="prose">
                <h3>What is missing</h3>
                <p>
                    No competition URL, paper, repository, or screenshot is
                    linked from this site. The figure is the engineering plate
                    used everywhere else for this project.
                </p>
            </div>
        </li>
    </Fragment>
</ProjectPage>
